-- ============================================================================
-- DR10 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Stimulation Design, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. The structure row is GENERATED from
-- the tier's manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: the fracture as a pressure problem. Net pressure over
-- closure, the plane strain modulus, the two classical two dimensional width
-- models, and the material balance that decides how long the job takes.
--
-- THE RESULT THE TIER IS BUILT ON, AND IT IS A DISAGREEMENT OF DIRECTION
-- RATHER THAN OF VALUE. PKN net pressure RISES with half-length while KGD net
-- pressure FALLS, across the whole sweep. The mechanism is in the compliance
-- terms: PKN divides by twice the fixed HEIGHT with a width going as the
-- quarter power of length, so it climbs; KGD divides by four times the
-- HALF-LENGTH with a width going as the square root, so the denominator
-- outruns the numerator. Two models of the same job that move opposite ways as
-- the design grows is why the model choice is a decision and not a preference.
-- Their widths differ by about a factor of 2.6 at the published conditions,
-- and the gap WIDENS with length, so the two agree least in exactly the long
-- contained geometry real designs aim for.
--
-- THE MOST USEFUL SINGLE FACT: the QUARTER POWER. Both models raise their
-- bracket to the power one quarter, so width is remarkably insensitive to rate
-- and viscosity. Sixteen times the rate buys twice the width. A designer who
-- wants a wider fracture has to change the rock, the height or the fluid
-- chemistry, because the pump will not do it.
--
-- AND THE BALANCE IS A FIXED POINT, NOT A FORMULA. The Nolte factor depends on
-- the efficiency, the efficiency depends on the pump time, and the pump time
-- depends on the factor, so the engine iterates to convergence. It converges
-- quickly because the factor only moves between 4/3 and pi/2 across the whole
-- efficiency range, so the map contracts hard. On the published case nearly
-- six volumes are pumped for every volume of fracture, which is what a
-- fracturing job actually is: mostly a leakoff problem.
-- ============================================================================

